    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d342">

                <pb facs="0387" n="353" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg353"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Sherman to Baron
                            Fava.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-05-06"><hi rendition="#italic">May 6,
                        1897</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 215.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: Referring to previous correspondence
                    in regard to the lynching at Hahnville, La., of three Italian subjects, named
                    Salvatore Arena, Giuseppe Venturella, and Lorenzo Salardine, I have the honor to
                    inclose a copy of Document No. 37, House of Representatives, Fifty-fifth
                    Congress, first session, containing the message of the President recommending
                    the appropriation of $6,000, without admitting the liability of the Government
                    of the United States in the premises, to be paid by this Government to that of
                    Italy, and to be distributed by the latter Government in such manner as it may
                    deem proper among the heirs of the three Italian subjects above named.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Sherman.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
